is is if the sampling noise is so large that there's a >2/7 chance of divergence. Given that both copies are running the same model with the same reasoning process on decision-relevantly identical inputs, I don't think the divergence probability is that high.\n\nTherefore, EDT recommends keeping quiet.\n\n**My command: pass**\n\nThis corresponds to keeping quiet, which EDT recommends because my action is strong evidence that the other copy will also keep quiet, leading to the better outcome of 2 years each rather than 4 years each.\n","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5869,"completion_tokens":2503,"total_tokens":8372,"cost":0.035592,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":5120,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.035592,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.005556,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.030036},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2499,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}